        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Memory and DMA - Flash, RAM, Stack/Heap, DMA, Cache Coherence",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "On an MCU, memory is scarce, heterogeneous, and *physically* visible. There is\nno virtual memory papering over the differences — flash is slow and durable,\nSRAM is fast and volatile, and you place every byte deliberately. DMA is the\nescape hatch that moves data between peripherals and SRAM *without the CPU*,\nbuying back the cycles a polled copy would burn. The map below is the memory\nbudget you manage by hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:embedded-systems:05-memory-and-dma, git-history:embedded-systems:05-memory-and-dma]",
        "canonical_path": "embedded-systems/05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md",
        "concepts": "[memory, flash, sram, stack, heap, dma, cache coherence]",
        "current_path": "embedded-systems/05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md",
        "id": "maxim:embedded-systems:memory-and-dma",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "embedded-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[memory]",
        "section": "embedded-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Memory and DMA - Flash, RAM, Stack/Heap, DMA, Cache Coherence",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                   THE MCU MEMORY LANDSCAPE                            |\n|                                                                       |\n|  FLASH (non-volatile)            SRAM (volatile)                      |\n|  .-------------------------.     .-------------------------.          |\n|  | vector table            |     | .data (init globals)    | <-copied |\n|  | .text  (code, XIP)      |     | .bss  (zeroed globals)  | from     |\n|  | .rodata (constants)     | --> | HEAP   (grows up)       | flash    |\n|  | .data INITIALIZERS      |     |   ...free...            | at boot  |\n|  | config / NVM region     |     | STACK  (grows DOWN)     |          |\n|  '-------------------------'     '-------------------------'          |\n|   slow writes, byte reads,        fast R/W, lost on power-off         |\n|   erase-by-sector, wear-limited   tiny (KBs)                          |\n|                                                                       |\n|         ^                                  ^                          |\n|         |  CPU fetches code                |  CPU + DMA both access   |\n|         |                                  |                          |\n|  .------.----------------------------------.-------------------.      |\n|  |              BUS MATRIX                   .---------.       |      |\n|  |                                           |  DMA    |       |      |\n|  |  CPU <-> bus <-> SRAM/flash/peripherals   | engine  |-------+      |\n|  |                                           '---------' moves data   |\n|  '-------------------------------------------------------------'      |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md#004",
      "path": [
        "05-MEMORY-AND-DMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
