        "title": "Memory and DMA - Flash, RAM, Stack/Heap, DMA, Cache Coherence",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read it as a budget.** Flash holds the program and constants; SRAM holds the\nmutable world. DMA shares the bus with the CPU to shuttle bytes between\nperipherals and SRAM autonomously. Every region has a fixed size you cannot\nexceed — overrun is not a page fault, it's corruption."
    },
